"""Meetings M32–M43 (Weeks 12–16): Studio 12, then the four exception weeks (D49).

Week 12 (nb12) — **Studio 12, Release and direct the next cycle**, and the last
studio of the semester. Monday teaches Lessons 38 and 39 (managing multiple AI
agents; conflicting agents and human escalation): scoped roles, dependency
wiring, and the price of agreement, run against a lapop_brazil draft claim the
room recomputes by hand. Wednesday teaches Lesson 40 (the final research and
AI-management portfolio) as the release audit itself — the stale-run rule, the
seven-row audit, the dossier manifest — and carries the week's SCORED colleague
audit. Friday IS Milestone 11 (Book Milestone 12 version 1). The order is the
lesson: you audit release BEFORE you release, and the Expo is the release.

Weeks 13–16 are the four date-driven exception weeks. They anchor no new lesson
and revisit what the studios already built. Week 13 (nb13) — the public test:
Monday's dress rehearsal and the stale-run recheck on a locked board, the Expo
on Tuesday, November 17 (required, graded, terminal), and Friday's reflection
studio where the captured questions are adjudicated into the CLAIM or only into
its DEFENSE (M12). There is no Wednesday meeting. Week 14 (nb14) — the
asynchronous Thanksgiving module: cold-run a PEER's anonymized package, red-team
it, run the required Reproducibility Auditor pass, and hand back a repair list
ranked by threat (M13, due Sunday night). This is Studio 11 practice on someone
else's work; the student's own package was built in Week 11. Week 15 (nb15) —
revision: Monday adjudicates the Expo criticism and the cold-run findings into
accept, rebut, or bound, and Wednesday repairs the package and proves it again
with a second clean run (M14 = Book Milestone 9 v2 + Book Milestone 11 v2).
Week 16 (nb16) — the close: live Evidence Defenses Monday and Wednesday, the
AI-management portfolio and the closed dossier, and Friday's submission
ceremony (M15, TERMINAL, no revision window). The agent lessons are TAUGHT in
Week 12 now, so Week 16 USES that skill rather than teaching it.

Fridays are studios (printed multiple-choice quiz + stand-up + milestone
kickoff and AI-supported work + revise/ledger/submit, no new topic content).
M37 is the asynchronous module and keeps its own free-form arc. Course
milestone M(n) presents a book Milestone version through the D49 bridge in
`planning/COURSE_BOOK_CROSSWALK.yml`: M11 → Milestone 12 v1; M12 → Milestone 10
v3 + Milestone 12 v2; M13 → Milestone 11 peer cold-run practice; M14 →
Milestone 9 v2 + Milestone 11 v2; M15 → Milestone 12 v3. M15 is terminal. The
Student Research Lead slots cover the seven Mon/Wed lectures here as slots
19–25; studios and the async module carry no SRL slot. The SCORED
Synthetic-Colleague audit runs once in this range, inside the Wednesday
laboratory of Week 12 (the last of the ten scored audits, Weeks 2–10 and 12);
Weeks 13 and 15 carry unscored continuation beats inside the Monday puzzle or
the Wednesday challenge, and Weeks 14 and 16 carry none. Colleague work never
appears on a Friday and is never assigned as homework.

Dataset numbers are recomputed from the shipped files: lapop_brazil.csv
(10,000 × 10) and foos_etal.csv (8,375 × 5), both from the rdss package
(Blair, Coppock & Humphreys, MIT License). RDSS chapter titles come from
`planning/RDSS_COVERAGE_MATRIX.md`; never invent a chapter. The AI tool named
in activities is the student's own AI assistant; GenAI Studio appears at its
designated role touchpoints (the orchestrator and reproducibility auditor at
M11, the poster critic at M12, the reproducibility auditor at M13, the research
note reviewer at M14). No fabricated citations anywhere.
"""

